# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-derived from css-flexbox-1 §9.2/§9.5/§9.7 with main and
# cross swapped (M9.9), before the code existed. Never regenerated.
#
# A column's main axis is the block axis, so every main-axis number in this
# file is a *height in lines* (PLAN.md's unit table: 16px or 1em to the line)
# and every cross-axis number is a width in cells. The cross axis is the easy
# one here: the container's content width is definite, so an item's width and
# its x are both settled before the item is built.
#
# Container 1 — the basics. `align-items` is unset, so `stretch`: each item's
# width is `auto` and fills the container's 20-cell content width, which is
# what makes `flex-direction: column` look like ordinary block flow.
#   "one"                     one line
#   "two three four five six" 20 cells to break in: "two three four five" is
#                             3+1+5+1+4+1+4 = 19, and " six" would make 23 —
#                             so two lines
#   "seven"                   one line
#   `flex-grow` is 0 initially, so nobody grows; the container is 1+2+1 = 4
#   lines tall and the items sit at y = 0, 1, 3.
#
# Container 2 — `gap: 1em 4em` is `<row-gap> <column-gap>`, and the two swap
#   roles with the axes. `row-gap` is the gutter *between rows*, which in a
#   column is between adjacent items: 1em vertical = 1 line. `column-gap` — 4em
#   = 8 cells — is the cross-axis gap, and a `nowrap` column has one line, so
#   it falls between nothing at all. Three 1-line items with a 1-line gap each
#   side of the middle one: y = 4, 6, 8, and the container is 3 + 2 = 5 tall.
#
# Container 3 — **the result most likely to be mistaken for a bug.** Both items
#   are `flex: 1` = `1 1 0`: grow 1, basis 0. The basis is a *height* now, and
#   the container's own `height` is `auto`, so its inner main size is not a
#   number the page gave — it is Σ(hypothetical outer main sizes), which is
#   what the items already are. §9.2 step 4 clamps each base of 0 by §4.5's
#   automatic minimum size, here the item's content height of 1 line, so the
#   hypothetical sizes are 1 and 1 and the container is 2. Free space is
#   therefore exactly zero: `flex-grow` has nothing to distribute and
#   `justify-content` would have nothing to move. The items keep their content
#   heights, at y = 9 and y = 10. A browser does the same thing.
#
# Container 4 — items are placed against the container's **content** edges, not
#   its border box. `padding: 1em 2em` is 1 line top and bottom, 4 cells left
#   and right, so the content box is x = 4, w = 20 - 8 = 12, and starts at
#   y = 11 + 1 = 12. Both items are 12 wide at x = 4. The box dump prints
#   content boxes, so the container's own line reads x=4 y=12 w=12 h=2 while
#   the flow it advances is the 4-line border box, putting the page at 15.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=15
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=15
    <div.col> flex column  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=4
      <div>  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=0 w=20 h=1
            #text "one"  x=0 y=0 w=3 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=2
        anonymous  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=2
          line  x=0 y=1 w=20 h=1
            #text "two three four five"  x=0 y=1 w=19 h=1
          line  x=0 y=2 w=20 h=1
            #text "six"  x=0 y=2 w=3 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=3 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=3 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=3 w=20 h=1
            #text "seven"  x=0 y=3 w=5 h=1
    <div.col.gapped> flex column  x=0 y=4 w=20 h=5
      <div>  x=0 y=4 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=4 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=4 w=20 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=4 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=6 w=20 h=1
            #text "b"  x=0 y=6 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=8 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=8 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=8 w=20 h=1
            #text "c"  x=0 y=8 w=1 h=1
    <div.col.grow> flex column  x=0 y=9 w=20 h=2
      <div>  x=0 y=9 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=9 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=9 w=20 h=1
            #text "x"  x=0 y=9 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=1
          line  x=0 y=10 w=20 h=1
            #text "y"  x=0 y=10 w=1 h=1
    <div.col.pad> flex column  x=4 y=12 w=12 h=2
      <div>  x=4 y=12 w=12 h=1
        anonymous  x=4 y=12 w=12 h=1
          line  x=4 y=12 w=12 h=1
            #text "p"  x=4 y=12 w=1 h=1
      <div>  x=4 y=13 w=12 h=1
        anonymous  x=4 y=13 w=12 h=1
          line  x=4 y=13 w=12 h=1
            #text "q"  x=4 y=13 w=1 h=1
